   = note: a borrow may not outlive what it points at (§6.1 rule 5); the value's storage ends at the close of the scope it was declared in
   = note: there is no lifetime syntax to widen: the fix is to return an owned value or an index, which is what `examples/21_compiler_shapes.science` §1 does

error[SC0330]: `s` is borrowed here and modified before the borrow ends
  --> tests/ui/regions/iterator_outlives_its_string.science:26:9
   |
25 |     for l in s.lines():
   |              --------- `s` is borrowed here, shared
   |              --------- the first borrow is still needed here
26 |         s be "zzzzzzzzzzzzzzzz"
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ ...and modified here, which needs it exclusively
   |
   = note: a shared borrow and an exclusive one cannot overlap (§6.1 rule 4)
   = note: the borrow ends at its last use, so moving the last use above the conflicting line is enough; binding what is needed before it is the other fix
